/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The inverse piezoelectric effect is the useful half of the story.
   - S is strain (ΔL/L, no unit); d33 is the piezoelectric charge coefficient in m/V, often quoted in pm/V; E is the electric field in V/m.
   - A stack actuator puts many thin ceramic layers mechanically in series and electrically in parallel.
   - A shape memory alloy (SMA) changes crystal phase with temperature.
   - The catch is heat.
   - Nitinol (NiTi) is the medical shape memory alloy.
   - Two conducting plates with a gap form a capacitor.
   - F is force in N; V is applied voltage in V; ε0 is 8.854 × 10−12 F/m; A is area in m²; g is gap in m.
   - A parallel-plate actuator is simple but has pull-in.
   - A comb drive avoids that in its travel direction.
*/
