/* book Worked example: Q: A Wheatstone bridge has R1 = 100 Ω in arm A–B, R2 = 200 Ω in arm A–C, R3 = 150 Ω in arm B–D and an unknown Rx in arm C–D. Find Rx at balance. A Maxwell bridge uses R2 = 1 kΩ, R3 = 10 kΩ and C1 = 0.1 µF in parallel with R1. Find the inductance L.
   1. Wheatstone balance: R1/R3 = R2/Rx, so Rx = R2R3/R1.
   2. Substitute: Rx = 200 × 150 / 100 = 300 Ω.
   3. Maxwell balance: L = R2R3C1.
   4. Convert C1: 0.1 µF = 0.1 × 10⁻⁶ F.
   5. Substitute: L = 1000 × 10 000 × 0.1 × 10⁻⁶ = 1 H.
   Answer:  */
